    "markdown": "# Website Style PRD — Aurora\n\n## Design Philosophy\nAurora captures the energy, optimism, and dynamic fluid nature of modern digital platforms. Built around luminous mesh gradients, frosted glass translucency, and vibrant ambient lighting, Aurora creates a sensation of depth, warmth, and cutting-edge forward momentum without sacrificing structural usability.\n\n## Overall Feel\nVibrant, futuristic, engaging, energetic, and visually exhilarating. Visiting an Aurora-styled page feels like stepping into a modern high-velocity tech product preview—dynamic, glowing with life, and full of interactive depth.\n\n## Target Audience\nModern AI startups, web3 platforms, creative developer tools, vibrant consumer apps, next-gen SaaS products, and fintech disruptors looking to convey innovation and velocity.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Ambient Luminosity: Use soft multi-stop mesh gradients and radial light halos to create atmospheric visual depth.\n2. Glassmorphic Surface Layering: Utilize backdrop blur filters and translucent borders to separate content tiers.\n3. High Energy Accents: Feature striking color gradients adapting to the chosen palette across badges, button highlights, and interactive triggers.\n4. Fluid Visual Hierarchy: Guide the eye through light intensity and color warmth rather than heavy dark containers.\n\n## Visual Direction\nLuminous dark or vibrant light canvases infused with multi-point radial light blooms adapting to the selected color palette. Cards feature frosted translucent glass surfaces bound by subtle glowing hairline borders. High color saturation on key callouts.\n\n## Layout System\nFluid responsive bento-grids and overlapping layered panels. Sections blend naturally into one another through ambient color transitions rather than abrupt hard horizontal rule dividers. Modular card groupings with variable aspect ratios.\n\n## Hero Section\nHigh-impact hero featuring dynamic multi-layer glowing typography over an ambient animated radial mesh background. Includes a floating translucent pill badge, a prominent preview device or glass module, and glowing primary CTAs.\n\n## Navigation\nGlassmorphic floating island header with rounded pill borders, glowing brand emblem, navigation links with subtle pill hover highlights, and a vibrant gradient action button.\n\n## Components\nTranslucent, glass-like UI controls. Segmented controls use sliding frosted pill selectors. Tooltips and dropdowns feature subtle glowing borders and deep drop-shadow halos. Floating action widgets with ambient glow effects.\n\n## Cards\nFrosted glass cards with multi-tier translucency, subtle top-edge light highlights, and soft gradient background glow on hover. Rounded corners enhance the fluid aesthetic.\n\n## Forms\nGlassmorphic input fields with translucent fills, subtle border glow on hover, and vibrant gradient focus rings. Floating input labels and clean validation badges.\n\n## Ctas\nRadiant palette-derived gradient buttons with subtle outer glow shadows. Smooth scale feedback and interactive sheen transitions on hover.\n\n## Imagery\nLuminous digital art, 3D refraction renders, vibrant product interface mockups placed over glowing mesh backdrops, and colorful glassmorphic UI cards.\n\n## Iconography\nDuotone or gradient-tinted vector line icons with glowing background aura chips. Icons feel integrated into the ambient light environment.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nFluid spring physics animations. Smooth gradient shifts, hover scale elevation, glowing ripple triggers, and smooth scroll parallax on background light blobs.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nOverlapping glass layers stack into clean vertical cards on mobile viewports. Frosted glass backgrounds maintain high contrast and readability over mobile canvases. Touch targets feature extra padding and glowing active feedback.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh contrast text overlays enforced across all ambient gradient zones. Background glass opacity adjusts dynamically to ensure solid legibility behind text blocks. Clear focus indicators for all interactive controls.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid dull monochromatic gray containers, harsh solid high-contrast rectangular boxes, static flat non-interactive blocks, low-contrast washed-out text on bright gradients, and rigid heavy-bordered tables.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Vibrant, luminous, mesh-gradient driven, and energetic.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always maintain high energy through dynamic layout or color accents.\n- Always use expressive, engaging interactions.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never become rigid or overly corporate.\n- Never use dull, lifeless static grids as the primary layout.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nAurora may evolve by refining its core traits: vibrant, luminous, mesh-gradient driven, and energetic.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like sterile enterprise grids.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Creative, Social, Consumer Apps\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Aurora but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Aurora identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Layered\n- **Animation Intensity:** Highly Expressive\n- **Illustration Presence:** Present\n- **Component Density:** Medium\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Standard\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 8/10**\nHigh visual energy and dynamic elements.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium**\nBalanced cognitive distribution.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 9/10\n- Density: 5/10\n- Decoration: 8/10\n- Structure: 7/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Aurora?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen generating a website in the Aurora style, emphasize ambient light, glowing gradients, and glassmorphic translucency. Incorporate subtle radial mesh background glows behind key sections. Use frosted glass cards with rounded corners. Style primary CTAs with radiant multi-stop gradients and soft glowing drop shadows. Include a floating glassmorphic navigation bar. Maintain high contrast text readability over all gradient surfaces.\n"
