    "markdown": "# Website Style PRD — Crystal\n\n## Design Philosophy\nCrystal is built around geometric precision, crisp facet lines, high visual clarity, and translucent refractive depth. It rejects soft organic blurs in favor of sharp, deliberate edge geometry, pristine typography, and prismatic light refractions.\n\n## Overall Feel\nCrisp, precise, modern, high-tech, razor-sharp, and sophisticated. Navigating a Crystal-styled site feels like examining an exquisitely cut gemstone under precision lighting.\n\n## Target Audience\nDeveloper tools, cloud infrastructure platforms, data engineering suites, security platforms, and high-precision financial software.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Geometric Facet Geometry: Structure content into crisp, angled tile containers.\n2. Prismatic Refraction: Utilize subtle light refractions along container borders.\n3. Razor-Sharp Clarity: Maintain crisp edge boundaries and high contrast typography.\n4. Precision Hierarchy: Group metrics and controls into structured multi-pane matrices.\n\n## Visual Direction\nCrystalline surfaces with crisp 1px border facets, sharp or micro-angled corners, and subtle refractive highlights adapting to the active palette.\n\n## Layout System\nPrecision grid matrices with explicit column boundaries, interlocking tile containers, and structured metric panels.\n\n## Hero Section\nPrecision hero with faceted headline typography, interactive 3D geometric node previews, and crisp outlined CTAs.\n\n## Navigation\nSleek top bar with sharp geometric dividers, status pills, and crisp line navigation items.\n\n## Components\nFaceted toggle groups, crisp segmented buttons, and structured status indicators.\n\n## Cards\nRefractive tile cards with sharp or micro-rounded corners, 1px border facets, and subtle surface fills.\n\n## Forms\nClean, structured input fields with crisp focus bounds and inline technical units.\n\n## Ctas\nHigh-precision solid or outlined CTAs featuring subtle edge highlight shifts on hover.\n\n## Imagery\n3D geometric renders, crystal structure diagrams, vector wireframes, and sharp technical screenshots.\n\n## Iconography\nSharp 1px linear geometric icons with crisp corner joins.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nInstantaneous, high-precision transitions. Sharp line extensions and crisp edge glows on hover.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nInterlocking tile grids re-align seamlessly from multi-column desktop panels into clean single-column stacks.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh-contrast text compliance across all refractive surfaces, explicit focus rings on all inputs.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid soft blurry background blobs, bubbly rounded pills, messy unaligned lists, and low-density spacing.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Prismatic, crisp, high-clarity, geometric, and modern.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always maintain precision and geometric clarity.\n- Always highlight interactive states explicitly.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never use soft, organic, or bubbly shapes unnecessarily.\n- Never obscure data behind heavy styling.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nCrystal may evolve by refining its core traits: prismatic, crisp, high-clarity, geometric, and modern.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like generic minimal templates.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Developer Tools, AI\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Crystal but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Crystal identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Layered\n- **Animation Intensity:** Moderate\n- **Illustration Presence:** Minimal\n- **Component Density:** High\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Advanced\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 7/10**\nBalanced and structured.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium High**\nHigh information density requires more attention.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 5/10\n- Density: 9/10\n- Decoration: 4/10\n- Structure: 9/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Crystal?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen generating a website in the Crystal style, emphasize sharp geometric alignment, crisp border facets, and refractive depth. Use structured tile matrices, sharp or micro-angled corners, and high-precision typography.\n"
