    "markdown": "# Website Style PRD — Vintage\n\n## Design Philosophy\nVintage pays homage to classic print craftsmanship, editorial publishing, and timeless typography. It pairs warm paper-textured canvases with elegant serif headlines, subtle ornamental rules, and rich editorial storytelling.\n\n## Overall Feel\nTimeless, warm, authentic, crafted, intellectual, and nostalgic. Vintage feels like holding a beautifully bound first-edition literary volume or a bespoke print magazine.\n\n## Target Audience\nArtisan crafts, heritage fashion brands, publishing houses, boutique wineries, historical archives, and craft culinary studios.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Craft Print Heritage: Treat the screen like a tactile printed paper page.\n2. Classic Serif Hierarchy: Pair commanding display serif titles with elegant body copy.\n3. Ornamental Divider Rules: Use fine divider lines and subtle typographic ornamentations.\n4. Warm Tonal Palette: Build upon warm off-white, sepia, or deep paper backdrops.\n\n## Visual Direction\nWarm off-white paper or deep sepia canvases with classic serif typography, fine hairline divider rules, and subtle stamp badges.\n\n## Layout System\nEditorial single and dual-column layouts with wide margins, drop caps, blockquote highlights, and centered chapter headers.\n\n## Hero Section\nClassic editorial hero featuring a large display serif title, elegant lead paragraph, subtle ornamental rule, and a refined CTA button.\n\n## Navigation\nTraditional top bar with centered brand serif logotype, fine bottom divider rule, and classic text navigation items.\n\n## Components\nClassic list items, ornamental divider rules, drop-cap paragraph leads, and stamp badges.\n\n## Cards\nPaper-like cards with fine 1px hairline borders, subtle background contrast, and zero heavy drop shadows.\n\n## Forms\nClean input fields with subtle bottom rules and elegant serif placeholder text.\n\n## Ctas\nRefined rectangular buttons with subtle border lines, solid fills, and classic typography.\n\n## Imagery\nClassic film photography, archival illustrations, warm monochrome portraits, and tactile print textures.\n\n## Iconography\nClassic thin line icons and hand-crafted vector badges.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nGentle fade and subtle page-turn transitions mimicking physical paper.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nEditorial text columns center gracefully with generous side margins on all devices.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh text contrast maintained against warm paper backdrops.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid harsh, uncalibrated colors, glossy glassmorphic cards, bouncy spring animations, and futuristic tech badges.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Timeless, editorial, warm, craft-driven, and nostalgic.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always maintain an unhurried, editorial pacing.\n- Always use deliberate, high-contrast typography.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never clutter the screen with high-density grids.\n- Never use cheap, generic component styling.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nVintage may evolve by refining its core traits: timeless, editorial, warm, craft-driven, and nostalgic.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like generic minimal templates.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Modern Digital Products\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Vintage but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Vintage identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Variable\n- **Animation Intensity:** Moderate\n- **Illustration Presence:** Minimal\n- **Component Density:** Medium\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Standard\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 4/10**\nBalanced and structured.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium**\nBalanced cognitive distribution.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 5/10\n- Density: 5/10\n- Decoration: 4/10\n- Structure: 7/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Vintage?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen generating a website in the Vintage style, emphasize classic print craftsmanship, serif typography, and warm paper canvases. Use fine hairline rules, editorial layouts, and timeless styling.\n"
