    "markdown": "# Website Style PRD — Flow\n\n## Design Philosophy\nFlow is a visual language built on continuity. It treats a website not as a series of disconnected pages or hard-edged blocks, but as a single, fluid stream of information. Sections bleed naturally into one another, elements respond organically to scroll and interaction, and the user’s journey is guided by seamless visual momentum rather than rigid structural boundaries.\n\n## Overall Feel\nFluid, seamless, continuous, organic, effortless, and connected. Navigating a Flow-styled site feels like moving downstream—natural, unobstructed, and instinctively guided.\n\n## Target Audience\nModern SaaS platforms, storytelling experiences, creative portfolios, product showcases, and consumer brands that want a frictionless, immersive journey.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Seamless Continuity: Eliminate hard horizontal dividers and abrupt background changes between sections.\n2. Organic Momentum: Use curved structural elements, overlapping layers, and soft asymmetric layouts to pull the eye downward.\n3. Fluid Transitions: Ensure elements morph, slide, or fade gracefully in response to interaction and scroll.\n4. Rhythmic Breathing: Balance dense content clusters with expansive whitespace to create a natural reading rhythm.\n\n## Visual Direction\nSoft, flowing surfaces adapting to the selected color palette. Elements overlap naturally. Backgrounds feature subtle, organic gradients or curved wave-like transitions instead of straight horizontal rules. Borders are soft and rounded.\n\n## Layout System\nFluid asymmetrical grids and overlapping content blocks. Sections blend together through interlocking shapes or gradient fades. Floating elements break the strict grid to create a sense of movement.\n\n## Hero Section\nImmersive hero layout that naturally guides the eye downward. Curved or diagonal bottom edges, floating contextual elements, and typography that flows seamlessly into the next section.\n\n## Navigation\nFloating or translucent top navigation that subtly shifts state on scroll, blending effortlessly with the changing backgrounds below it.\n\n## Components\nRounded, organic UI components. Progress indicators are fluid bars or smooth rings. Toggles and sliders feature liquid-like, smooth transitions.\n\n## Cards\nSoftly rounded cards that appear to float organically on the canvas. Borders are nonexistent or extremely subtle, relying instead on soft elevation and spacing.\n\n## Forms\nSeamless input fields with rounded edges, soft focus rings, and inline validations that fade in organically without shifting the layout.\n\n## Ctas\nFully rounded pill buttons or smooth rectangular buttons with generous radii. Hover states feature smooth, liquid-like color or scale transitions.\n\n## Imagery\nImages placed in rounded or organically shaped masks. Parallax scrolling and subtle scale effects keep imagery feeling alive and connected to the scroll rhythm.\n\n## Iconography\nSoft, rounded vector icons with a flowing, unbroken stroke style. Icons feel organic rather than sharply geometric.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nSmooth scroll-linked animations, liquid easing curves, and organic reveal effects. Interactions feel continuous and responsive, never abrupt or mechanical.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nFluid layouts scale gracefully, with overlapping elements stacking naturally on smaller screens while maintaining curved section boundaries.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh-contrast text and clear focus indicators are maintained despite the soft, fluid visual aesthetic.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid rigid grid lines, hard horizontal section dividers, sharp geometric corners, sudden jarring transitions, and boxed-in, disconnected content silos.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Fluid, continuous, seamless, organic, and effortlessly connected.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always use fluid, natural spacing and transitions.\n- Always prioritize a calm, continuous user journey.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never use harsh, rigid containers or sharp cutoffs.\n- Never rush animations or interactions.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nFlow may evolve by refining its core traits: fluid, continuous, seamless, organic, and effortlessly connected.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like generic minimal templates.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Health, Wellness, Education\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Flow but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Flow identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Variable\n- **Animation Intensity:** Moderate\n- **Illustration Presence:** Minimal\n- **Component Density:** Medium\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Standard\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 4/10**\nBalanced and structured.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium**\nBalanced cognitive distribution.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 5/10\n- Density: 5/10\n- Decoration: 4/10\n- Structure: 4/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Flow?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen generating a website in the Flow style, prioritize seamless continuity and organic momentum. Use overlapping layers, soft rounded containers, and curved or gradient section transitions to eliminate hard boundaries. Implement smooth, fluid transitions and ensure the layout guides the user's eye naturally down the page.\n"
