    "markdown": "# Website Style PRD — Mosaic\n\n## Design Philosophy\nMosaic brings the richness of editorial magazine publishing and bento tile composition to modern websites. It interlocks content cards of varying aspect ratios, feature callouts, quotes, and visual media into a harmonious grid composition.\n\n## Overall Feel\nRich, curated, engaging, intellectual, dynamic, and editorial. Mosaic feels like flipping through an award-winning digital culture magazine.\n\n## Target Audience\nDigital publications, brand storytelling hubs, media portfolios, content archives, and curated marketplace collections.\n\n## Core Design Principles\n1. Rich Content Tiles: Combine text, metrics, media, and quotes in interlocking grid containers.\n2. Varied Aspect Ratio Hierarchy: Highlight key feature stories with large hero tiles.\n3. At-a-Glance Scannability: Structure cards with bold headlines, author bylines, and category tags.\n4. Clean Grid Boundaries: Maintain consistent alignment gaps between all mosaic tiles.\n\n## Visual Direction\nClean light or surfaces adapting to the selected color palette with interlocking mosaic tiles, fine hairline borders, category tag badges, and rich media overlays.\n\n## Layout System\nMulti-column mosaic grids with interlocking 1x1, 2x1, 2x2, and vertical span tiles.\n\n## Hero Section\nFeatured mosaic grid hero highlighting a primary cover story tile surrounded by supporting secondary story cards and live category filters.\n\n## Navigation\nEditorial top bar with category dropdowns, search trigger, and publication logotype.\n\n## Components\nCategory chips, author byline tags, reading time indicators, and media tiles.\n\n## Cards\nInterlocking mosaic cards with clean hairline borders, subtle surface fills, and integrated media thumbnails.\n\n## Forms\nClean search and newsletter subscription inputs with inline submission triggers.\n\n## Ctas\nRefined rectangular or rounded CTAs featuring clear directional arrows.\n\n## Imagery\nEditorial photojournalism, portrait photography, architectural imagery, and curated artwork.\n\n## Iconography\nClean linear vector icons.\n\n## Motion And Interaction\nSmooth scale and shadow elevation on tile hover.\n\n## Responsive Behaviour\nInterlocking mosaic tiles re-align smoothly into clean single or dual-column mobile feeds.\n\n## Accessibility\nHigh-contrast text overlays maintained across all photo and media tiles.\n\n## Things To Avoid\nAvoid messy non-aligned tile gaps, unreadable micro-text on background images, and chaotic uncurated layouts.\n\n## Style Invariants\n### Must Always\n- Always align with the core philosophy: Dynamic, editorial grid, rich content tiles, and magazine-driven.\n- Maintain structural integrity and clear hierarchy.\n- Prioritize user experience over unrequested aesthetic flourishes.\n- Always maintain an unhurried, editorial pacing.\n- Always use deliberate, high-contrast typography.\n\n### Must Never\n- Never imitate conflicting styles.\n- Never compromise accessibility for aesthetics.\n- Never introduce unprompted visual clutter.\n- Never clutter the screen with high-density grids.\n- Never use cheap, generic component styling.\n\n## Evolution Rules\nMosaic may evolve by refining its core traits: dynamic, editorial grid, rich content tiles, and magazine-driven.. It must never evolve toward conflicting paradigms like generic minimal templates.\n\n## Compatibility Matrix\n**Excellent For:** Modern Digital Products\n**Good For:** Broad Use Cases\n**Acceptable For:** General purpose applications\n**Avoid For:** Mismatched domain constraints\n\n## Adaptation Strategy\nFor high trust or enterprise domains, maintain the core identity of Mosaic but reduce unrequested visual noise, ensure highly legible data boundaries, and prioritize clear navigation over aesthetic flourishes.\n\n## Conflict Resolution\nWhen generating UI, adhere to the following strict priority hierarchy:\n1. **Project Intent & Core Functionality**\n2. **Accessibility Requirements**\n3. **Platform Guidelines**\n4. **Style PRD Invariants**\n5. **Typography & Color Palette Constraints**\n6. **Optional Decorations**\n\n## Ai Failure Criteria\nValidation fails if the design loses its Mosaic identity, specifically if it violates the invariants or drifts toward a generic baseline.\n\n## Quantifiable Metrics\n- **Whitespace Usage:** Variable\n- **Border Usage:** Variable\n- **Elevation:** Variable\n- **Animation Intensity:** Moderate\n- **Illustration Presence:** Minimal\n- **Component Density:** Medium\n- **Navigation Complexity:** Standard\n\n## Visual Entropy\n**Score: 4/10**\nBalanced and structured.\n\n## Cognitive Load\n**Level: Medium**\nBalanced cognitive distribution.\n\n## Style Fingerprint\n- Whitespace: 6/10\n- Motion: 5/10\n- Density: 5/10\n- Decoration: 4/10\n- Structure: 7/10\n\n## Regression Testing\nGenerate identical benchmark products (e.g., Dashboard, Portfolio). **Pass Criteria:** The style's multidimensional fingerprint is immediately recognizable. Hierarchy and density remain intact regardless of domain.\n\n## Ai Evaluation Framework\nScore generated UIs (1-10) on:\n- **Style Fidelity:** Unmistakably Mosaic?\n- **Hierarchy & Flow:** Visual weight distributed per principles?\n- **Density Accuracy:** Matches fingerprint?\n- **Platform Correctness:** Native Web/Android paradigms?\n- **Prompt Determinism:** Avoids hallucinated generic flair?\n\n## AI Generation Instructions\nWhen generating a website in the Mosaic style, emphasize editorial magazine tile layouts, interlocking card compositions, category tags, and rich content hierarchy.\n"
